# Files that run on Linux must keep LF endings even when checked out on Windows,
# where core.autocrlf=true would otherwise rewrite them to CRLF. A CRLF shell
# script fails on Linux with "\r: command not found" (or "not found" for a CRLF
# shebang), and a CRLF entrypoint copied into an image fails when the container
# starts. Dockerfiles are pinned too: a RUN line continued with a trailing
# backslash breaks when the backslash is followed by a CR.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
